/*
  04_missing_sequences.sql  -  SEQUENCE objects, which the SSMS 'Generate Scripts' export leaves out.
  Definitions (type, MIN/MAX, CACHE) as on production, from the snapshot of 2026-10-21 (sys.sequences of every
  database on the production instance). START WITH = the production current value + 1 on that day, so local
  numbers do not collide with real ones. Only databases that exist on this instance are touched; existing
  sequences are left as they are. Run from any database (uses <db>.sys.sp_executesql). Idempotent.

  Production cut-over: a backup/restore carries the sequences with their current values, so this file is not
  needed there. If data is moved any other way, re-create them from a fresh snapshot taken in the cut-over
  window (SELECT name, TYPE_NAME(user_type_id), start_value, increment, minimum_value, maximum_value,
  is_cycling, is_cached, cache_size, current_value FROM sys.sequences) - never from these numbers.

  'NOT ON PRODUCTION' stand-ins: procedures use these sequences but production has no such object, so those
  procedures fail there (see database/README.md); they exist here only so the scripts compile and run locally.
*/
